{
  "dom_id": "step-q130995",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "For the differential equation ${y}^{\u2033}-6{y}^{\u2032}+5y=9{e}^{2x},$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{\u2033}+b(x){y}^{\u2032}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{\u2033}+b(x){y}^{\u2032}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}-6{y}^{\u2032}+5y=0.\n$$",
